Z||000000||fropuff||05-19-2001||11:48 PM||||Hey guys.  I am going to get my new front fascia and ground effects painted soon, and I was thinking of keeping the GFX the stock '86 GT silver.  Now when I was surfing one forum members' website, I think I may have changed my mind and go with the red.  I would also get the wheels stripped and painted black.  I may also get a GT wing and have it painted red also, as well as the mirrors.  I know what you're thinking..."Oh my goodness, the kid's an '88 GT poser!  What a little ricer SOB!"  I know.  Who cares.  Not me.  I've always wanted an '88 GT, but I haven't had the $ to get one.  I guess you could call it my dream car.  If you want to see the web page that inspired my thinking, it's at: <A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>   I really like the picture of it now, but mine would look like the "before" picture, just with red mirrors.  This guy is my new hero.  I'm sorry that I don't know his name, but he should be very proud of this car.  I just hope he doesn't hate me for copying his car.  Oh, please let me know what you think of my ricer ways.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks a lot. <BR>||||reg||10
Z||000001||fropuff||05-19-2001||11:50 PM||||By the way, my '86 GT is currently red w/ the silver GFX.  I forgot to say that it's red, but it is.  Now if it was white or neon green, you could call me a ricer.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks.||||reg||1
Z||000002||sjp777||05-19-2001||11:53 PM||||You mean like the car in my sig below?<P>Thank you<P>Feel free to copy away. Imitation is the sincerest form of flattery.    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"><P>P.S. I don't think there is anything rice about my car. The only sticker it has is the ASU sticker in the back window. Go Devils!<P>------------------<BR>     <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_1.jpg">    <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A><P><p>[This message has been edited by sjp777 (edited 05-20-2001).]||||reg||10
Z||000003||fropuff||05-20-2001||01:20 AM||||Yep, that's the one!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  You really have a nice car.  I think a mock '88 GT will look sweet.  I really like the black wheels on em.  I also really like your wheels now, but I don't have nearly the $ to buy em.  And I have new tires anyway.  I might lower mine ~1.5" if I can.  I have a long list of to-dos.  The reason I want the red mirrors is because I hate the look of em now.  I hate the little triangular plate in front of the window and the mirrors.  I think the mirrors should go there, but they can't.  If the mirrors were red, it'll look better, IMO.  That's enough talkin for me.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks for lettin me copy you!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  <P>PS: I didn't mean that your car was rice...I meant that some people say that making your Fiero look like another is ricey.  (Like a coupe looking like a Formula)  I don't think it's ricey though.  A lot of the things between the '86 and '88 GTs are similar anyway.  I do have one sticker on mine...a dog pissin on MR2!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
Z||000004||sjp777||05-20-2001||01:43 AM||||I've been looking at late model Grand AMs lately and I've noticed their mirrors are painted to match body, have a really nice design and they mount on that triangle piece that is remarkably similar in size and shape to the Fiero piece.<P>Anybody try to retro-fit them on the Fiero?<P>------------------<BR>    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/890sm_2.jpg">   <BR><A HREF="http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/" TARGET=_blank>http://www.geocities.com/fiero88gt1/</A>||||reg||1
