Z||000007||fropuff||05-20-2001||11:51 AM||||Oh, well thanks, Pontiaddict!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  I wasn't aware you told me.  You did not, however, tell me to paint the mirrors.  That's okay, I'll let that one slide.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  As far as the mirrors go, I was planning on trying to modify some mirrors to fit in the triangular piece, but I found out that it probably wouldn't work.  The mirrors would have to be very short width-wise, because the door glass needs to swing an arc when you open the door.  The mirrors could only be like 4 or 5 inches wide to work.  Unless you like rolling the windows down to open the door.   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">  Thanks for the help.||||reg||1
Z||000008||fropuff||05-20-2001||12:27 PM||||Okay, I've got a question about refinishing the 15" GT lace wheels.  If I go with red ground effects, I will also go to a black wheel, not the silver that is already on there.  I have already stripped the clear off the outer part of the rim, but I left the painted area.  If I go black, can I just sand the silver areas so it'll hold on to new paint?  I have heard that underneath the paint, the rim is very rough.  I won't have the time to sand all of it, so I was wondering if I can just sand and repaint em?  Thanks!||||reg||1
Z||000009||fropuff||05-23-2001||04:21 PM||||Well, I think I have made up my mind.  I think...  Anyway, I think I'll go with the red GFX, wing, mirrors, and black wheels.  I will repaint all the black stuff black, and tint the tail lamps, marker lights, and my back-up lights.  I will also tint the windows and get some tinted GT sail panels.  I still am wondering if I can just scuff up the paint on my wheels instead of stripping everything, and repainting them.  Can I???  Thanks a lot!!!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
